# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values for the backend you use.
#   cp .env.example .env
# aicommit reads these from the environment; it does not load .env automatically,
# so `export`/`source` them or use a tool like direnv / dotenv.

# --- NVIDIA NIM (default backend: free cloud) -------------------------------
# Create a free account at https://build.nvidia.com (about 2 minutes), then
# generate a key. It starts with "nvapi-". Real keys are ~70 chars of base64.
NVIDIA_API_KEY=nvapi-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

# Optional: override the chat model used on NIM.
# Default: meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct
# NIM_MODEL=meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct

# Optional: override the NIM base URL (rarely needed).
# NIM_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1

# --- Ollama (fully local backend) -------------------------------------------
# Install from https://ollama.com, then: `ollama serve` and `ollama pull llama3.1`.
# No API key is required. Select it per run with `--backend ollama`, or set
# `backend: ollama` in .aicommit.yaml.
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434
# Default model when backend is ollama:
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.1

# --- No model at all ----------------------------------------------------------
# `aicommit --backend local` drafts rule-based messages from the diff: no key,
# no network, not AI. It is also what the git hook falls back to when the
# backend above fails (see AICOMMIT_HOOK_FALLBACK).

# --- aicommit settings (optional; .aicommit.yaml is the usual place) ---------
# These environment variables override the config file.
# AICOMMIT_BACKEND=nim            # nim | ollama | local
# AICOMMIT_MODEL=
# AICOMMIT_LANGUAGE=en            # en | es
# AICOMMIT_ALLOWED_TYPES=feat,fix,docs,style,refactor,perf,test,build,ci,chore,revert
# AICOMMIT_EMOJI=false
# AICOMMIT_SUBJECT_MAX_LENGTH=72
# AICOMMIT_PR_BASE=main
# AICOMMIT_MAX_DIFF_CHARS=12000
# AICOMMIT_TEMPERATURE=0.3
# AICOMMIT_IGNORE_PATHS=src/generated/,*.pb.go
# AICOMMIT_HOOK_FALLBACK=true
